.TH DANBY-CHAOS 1
.SH NAME
danby-chaos \- Lorenz chaotic convection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/chaos
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/chaos
is an interactive live simulation of Lorenz chaotic convection.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
X'=sigma(Y-X); Y'=X(rho-Z)-Y; Z'=XY-beta Z.
.PP
sigma, rho, and beta control the Lorenz system; X, Y, and Z are abstract convection state variables.
.SH DISPLAY
The upper x-z projection displays two trajectories beginning only
10^-6 units apart.  They initially overlap, then separate and eventually
occupy the two-lobed strange attractor.  The lower plot shows
log10 of their Euclidean separation against time, making sensitive dependence
visible before it can be distinguished in the phase portrait.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the main view to change initial X. The bottom tracks set sigma, rho, and beta.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
Both states are advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver using identical timesteps.  The model module's
equilibria are checked by the automated Danby model test.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/chaos.b
.PP
.B /appl/danby/lorenz.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)
